Job Description:
Job Description
Intern – HR & Administration
This is a six months Internship position under the HR & Administration function at KAM.
Internship Purpose:
To enable the intern gain on-the-job HR and administration skills while supporting the HR team in delivering administrative and HR services at KAM.
Responsibilities
Reporting to the HR & Administration Manager at KAM, the HR Intern will be responsible for;
Support generation of routine reports especially on implementation and tracking of HR practices – Training, policy compliance, staff facilitation etc;
Assist the HR function in basic recruitment processes and related desk work;
Support the HRM in employees inductions for effective staff placement;
Support in maintenance of employee information by entering and updating employment and status-changes database as may be assigned;
Support in coordinating staff engagement / motivation initiatives and welfare activities;
Assist in maintenance of the HR basic filing system as may be assigned;
Contribute to team efforts by accomplishing HR and Administration results as required;
Perform other HR support tasks as may be assigned by supervisor or CEO from time to time.
Qualifications
Bachelor’s degree in HR or a degree in related field with a Diploma in HR Management;
Knowledge of HR administration processes is critical;
Good communication skills, outgoing personality and good reporting skills;
Person of integrity and ability to maintain confidentiality;
Fast to understand concepts with keen attention to detail and willingness to learn;
Ability to multi-task and get things done to a good conclusion;
Excellent planning and organizational skills
English (Spoken: fluent | Written: fluent)

Mwananchi Communications Limited, a subsidiary of Nation Media Group and publishers of leading Tanzania newspapers, Mwananchi, Mwanaspoti, The Citizen and various online products is looking for motivated and highly experienced individuals to fill the position of Sales Coordinator, Mwanaspoti Kenya.
The Job holder will support the NMG- Kenya sales team in developing, coordinating, monitoring and evaluating sales and marketing strategies aimed at increasing market share and sales revenue for Mwanaspoti Kenya newspaper.
Responsibilities
Identify and execute the identified sales opportunities in the market in order to achieve the sales budget;
Respond and pre-screen potential new clients/partners as well as assist end-users seeking partnerships across the country;
Maintain Customer Accounts timely and accurately with the most current information;
Nurtures business relationships with business partners;
Assists in the identification of strategic business partners that are in line with Mwanaspoti brand;
Grows long-term relationships with clients and capitalises on equity and partnership opportunities;
Ability to seek and develop new business and maximize all possible opportunities to increase sales.
Accurately forecasts revenue, profitability and sets expectations upward regarding revenue and profitability projections.
Qualifications
BSc/BA in Business Administration or relevant field; certification in sales or marketing will be an asset;
Experience in using MS office tools with excellent verbal and written communication skills
Team player with high level dedication and integrity;
3 to 5 years working experience as sales coordinator or administrative positions with an aptitude in problem solving;
Self-motivated, agile, flexible person with skills and knowledge of customer care services.
go to method of application »

Nation Media Group seeks to recruit experienced and self-motivated individuals to fill the position of Territory Sales Executive in the Circulation department:
Reporting to the Area Business Partners, the Territory Sales Executives will work with the Circulation team to maximise on newspapers' sales opportunities through accurate orders setting, close customer contact and feedback from the distribution area.
Key responsibilities
Achieving revenue and volume budgets;
Managing Returns /unsold newspapers;
Organising and driving circulation operations through field sales visits to vendors and agents in order to maximize on opportunities for copy sales;
Ensuring efficient management of the value chain;
Identifying potential sales outlets and liaising with NCD for correct deliveries;
Reviewing weekly payments with the distributor, collecting payment cheques on due dates and ensuring the cheques reach the Circulation Accountant;
Organising client relationship programmes in liaison with Area Business Partner, the distributor, agents and vendors.
Required Skills:
Diploma in Business Management or a business related field;
At least 3 years' experience in FMCG 'environment;
A valid riding license;
Analytical, self -driven and love to be measured on performance;
Demonstrable passion for sales and marketing;
Understanding of the dynamics and complexity of print sales and circulation;
People management skills.
Note: We shall only contact the shortlisted applicants.

The ideal candidate for the Finance Director role is be self- driven, has a strong work ethic with a high standard of attention to detail and quality. The incumbent will be a member of the AECF senior management team and will be responsible for providing oversight and leading the work of the Finance function in line with the AECF strategic goals. The role holder will have overall responsibility for managing and reporting AECF’s finances.
Key Responsibilities:
Direct and oversee all aspects of the Finance & Accounting functions of AECF;
Provide timely and accurate analysis of budgets, financial reports and financial trends in order to assist the Board and senior management team in executing their responsibilities, and ensuring that all tax, audit and compliance aspects are addressed in timely manner;
Ensure AECF’s compliance with relevant accounting standards and reporting in AECF’s countries of operation;
Oversee the company’s transaction processing systems, monitoring cash balances, developing cash projection processes, and providing timely financial information and reports;
Ensure timely, accurate and transparent financial reporting to donors and other partners as required;
Oversee the production of cash flow reports, annual budget, and forecasts working effectively with Senior Management Team;
Ensure that effective internal controls are in place and ensure compliance with IFRS and all applicable laws and rules for financial and tax reporting;
Develop financial and tax strategies, together with performance measures and monitoring systems that support the AECF’s strategic direction
Support the acquisition of capital assets and ensure that assets are properly recorded, amortized, and disposed of as appropriate;
Oversee the management of the budget ensuring targets are met without exceeding budget allocations and develop procedures to measure cost effectiveness including variance reporting;
As a member of the senior management team, be central in the development and implementation of the AECF strategy, corporate culture and values;
Management of the Finance team and accountability for its performance and decisions;
Required qualifications, experience and skills:
Masters’ degree in accounting, finance, or business administration;
Certified Public Accountant (CPA) or hold an equivalent professional accounting qualification e.g. ACCA;
8+ years working experience in a senior role, including responsibility for financial management and control, at least part of which should have been in sub-Saharan Africa;
Knowledge of donor reporting processes specifically bilateral donors;
Ability to create a strong vision for the team and inspire others to greater performance, professional standards and results
Ability to engage with a diverse range of teams and partners and comfortable building strong working relationships.
Encourages a high-performing culture in the team.
Fluency in English with French being desirable.
The AECF is an Equal Opportunity Employer.
If you believe you can clearly demonstrate your abilities to meet the relevant criteria for the role, please submit your application quoting in the subject line the Job Title “Finance Director – AECF/FD/2019”, and attach a detailed CV, e-mail address and telephone contacts. To be considered, your application must be received by Friday 11th October 2019 addressed to: recruitment@aecfafrica.org.

Job Description
Place within the organization
Endorses the mission and vision of KidsCare Kenya;
Is a member of the team of KidsCare Kenya;
Is responsible for the assistance, guidance, and support of children with special abilities within their assigned locations;
Is the face of KidsCare within the locations and households he/she is attached to;
Is attached to children with special abilities (CSA) programs and responsible for activities that KidsCare is doing for Children with special abilities (CSA) and their environment, including guiding the caretakers of Children with Special Abilities;
Strengthen the position of mentally challenged children and youngsters, by doing homecare, creating awareness to the community, advise the support groups, activate the stakeholders and facilitate special services and advocate on the rights of CSA through the community;
Is accountable for the physical and emotional progress of the children in the program in their locations;
Are part of the social work department and the team members support the other team members by giving feedback and helping to give solutions for challenges.
Reporting to
works under the supervision of the head of departments CSA and CBHB;
reports to the Manager CSA.
Job content
Stimulates the involvement of the families and the community in realizing a better position of CSA in society;
Sits in on behalf of the locational social worker when need be;
Helps in giving information in KLT meetings concerning the progress in CSA and SSU programs.
Give guidance to CSA caregivers to promote the independence of CSA both mental and physical.
Strengthen the social-economic status of the CSA through capacity building the caregivers.
Improve the status of children with special abilities through the caregivers and society by advocating on the rights of CSA hence giving them a better future.
Has good contact with SSU and work together to improve on the functional skills and independence of CSA in the units.
Collect, plan and monitor all relevant information and make reports during periodic evaluations.
Implements children with special ability program within the locations.
Make a home visit to CSA to know their living circumstances and improve their living conditions at home.
Writing an individual care plan and monitoring the progress of a CSA (and their family) according to the individual care plan
Assists the locational social workers and OT in doing mobilization to children with disabilities within their locations to join Therapies and Special school units.
Increase the awareness of expertise and involvement of stakeholders.
Presenting KidsCare in events in the community
Job profile
Diploma in Social Work/Community Development.
Have knowledge of disabilities in children.
At least two years of experience in working with children with disabilities.
Have experience in working on with the community
Is able to ride a motorbike and have a valid license;
Computer literate;
Have knowledge of counseling;
Able to work independently;
Is able to work under difficult circumstances, help children with specials abilities and their caretakers;
Is able to take feedback and ready to learn.
Have good therapeutic skills (e.g. counseling, consultation skills, coaching, educating)
Skills:
Motivated and willing to work with Children with special abilities and their families.
Be proactive and goal-oriented.
Able to handle him/herself well in term of conflict and be able to give solutions.
Well organized and willing to take responsibilities
Flexible and ready to take other task requested by managers or management team
Good in communication can address community and express him/herself.
A good team player.
Good in written and spoken English.
Values, competences, management skills and job related competences
Values
caring;
better world;
together;
achievement;
capable;
leadership.
Competences
customer care;
teamwork/cooperation;
communication;
drive and enthusiasm;
leadership.
Management skills
strategy & organization;
general management & administration skills;
ability to provide leadership & guidance;
ability to ensure quality brand standards are applied;
research and development;
marketing.
Job related competences
