Job Description
Description of job:
Responsible for the key relationship interfaces of the four major telecommunication operators in the Kenyan region of East Africa (Kenya & East Africa key countries) and customer maintenance, according to the company's strategic requirements and business needs, dig the needs of operators and cooperate with the company's product promotion;
Responsible for business development with relevant communication supervision units such as Kenya CCK, anti-telecom fraud police department, familiar with business communication, excellent customer development and business cooperation experience.
Responsible for the sales policy of the regional operators and the related sales work;
Complete business negotiations independently, supervise the implementation of business cooperation plans, and promote business cooperation.
Fully grasp the competing product information, design and implement the corresponding strategy.
Job requirements:
Bachelor degree or above, more than 3 years working experience;
Fully familiar with the operator's business and related operational processes;
Excellent business negotiation skills and resource integration capabilities, familiar with local operators' channel systems at all levels, and operators' work background is preferred;
Have strong logical thinking ability and writing skills.
Strong market development ability, high negotiation skills, and good customer relationship management capabilities;
Have good business network resources for operators.

Company Details:
In developing our campaign strategies and policies we take great care to reflect our fundamental respect for democratic principles while seeking out solutions that will promote global social equity.
Our vision is an Africa where people live in harmony with nature in a peaceful state of environmenta...read morel and social justice.
Our mission is to work with others to foster environmental consciousness whereby Africa's people seek social and economic prosperity in ways that protect the environment for the benefit of humans, the planet, and the future.
Our core values are reflected in all our environmental work, worldwide.
These are:
 We 'bear witness' to environmental destruction in a peaceful, non-violent manner;
 We use non-violent confrontation to raise the level and quality of public debate;
 In exposing threats to the environment and finding solutions we have no permanent allies or adversaries;
 We ensure our financial independence from political or commercial interests;
 We seek solutions for, and promote open, informed debate about society's environmental choices.
In developing our campaign strategies and policies we take great care to reflect our fundamental respect for democratic principles and to seek solutions that will promote global social equity.

Job Description:
The Head of Payment Services Policy Development & Data Analysis is responsible for overseeing the development of policy that govern the National Payment Systems (NPS) as well as conduct research and analysis of the performance of the national payment systems.
Responsibilities
Contribute as appropriate to the performance of National Payment Systems functions and to the overall achievement of CBK’s strategic objectives;
Guide and support implementation of an integrated information management system for electronic submission and processing of NPS returns;
Carry out research and analysis on emerging issues e.g. FinTechs;
Continuously review and propose updates to NPS policy framework, law and regulations in line with international best practices;
Identify new areas for inclusive financing and recommend actions for policy formulation;
Coordinate all activities related to financial inclusion as well as sensitization and training on the new payment platforms;
Monitor industry developments and continuously update NPS returns templates;
Ensure timely submission of NPS returns and provide periodic standard analytical reports;
Implement an integrated information system for electronic submission of NPS returns;
Perform analysis and verification of payment data and update the statistics on the CBK website;
Design consumer awareness programs;
Overseeing training of staff in the Section to enable the staff perform in line with Bank guidelines;
Qualifications
A degree in Business, Economics, Banking, Finance, Insurance, Law, Mathematics, Computer Science or related field of study;
Possession of a Master’s degree in a related field of study is an added advantage;
Possession of Professional qualification in a related field of study is an added advantage.
Work Experience
Minimum of eight (8) years’ work experience in Banking Operations and Payment Systems, Financial Services, Economics, Accounting or similar operations, with five (5) years in a supervisory position.
Competencies
Technical Competencies
Good knowledge of data analysis methods such as predictive analytics, mapping, collecting data from multiple data systems on premises and cloud-based data sources;
Ability to perform effective querying involving multiple tables and sub-queries;
Experience in using analytical concepts and statistical techniques- hypothesis development, designing tests, analyzing data and drawing conclusions;
Experience building and leading quantitative analyses and response and risk models;
Knowledge and understanding of banking laws and regulations as well as Central Banking operations;
Experience working with large data sets and advanced analytical tools, programs and systems;
Behavioral/General Competencies
Excellent leadership skills and people management skills; including performance management, coaching & mentoring;
Good interpersonal skills with ability to build consensus, alliances and collaborative relationships with stakeholders;
Strategic thinking, problem solving and decision making skills;
Ability to demonstrate CBK’s core values.
